Modern Text

A Plug-In for Mill. Put it in the "Mill Plug-Ins" folder.

  Markdown    .md and .markdown, text/markdown: CommonMark, with tables
  Gemtext     .gmi and .gemini, text/gemini: Gemini's text

Both show as pages: headings, paragraphs, lists, quotes, code, links,
images, and Markdown's tables. Text is read as UTF-8 unless the server
names another character set (ISO 8859-1 and Mac Roman are known), and
shown in Mac Roman. Relative links go by the page's own address.

Markdown: ATX and setext headings, paragraphs, block quotes, bullet and
numbered lists inside each other, fenced and indented code, thematic
breaks, hard line breaks, HTML blocks and inline HTML (passed on to
Mill), emphasis and strong emphasis, code spans, inline and reference
links and images, autolinks, backslash escapes, entities, and GitHub's
pipe tables. Simplified:

  - A list is tight until a blank line comes between its items (or
    between two blocks in one); its paragraphs are <P>s from there on.
  - Tabs are made spaces only in a line's indentation.
  - Link titles aren't shown (HTML 3.2 has nowhere to put them).
  - A reference link whose definition comes later waits for it, with
    what follows, up to 4K of page; past that it goes out as the text
    it was, and the definition, when it comes, is listed at the page's
    end. 48 definitions at most.
  - A paragraph over 4K goes out in parts, cut at line ends; emphasis
    and links can't span a cut, and such a paragraph can't become a
    setext heading or a table. A line over 1K is cut too: the rest
    continues the paragraph or code block it is in.
  - Lists and quotes nest 24 deep (a list and its item count two);
    deeper markers are text. A run of * or _ takes part in 6 matches
    at most, and runs over 100 are text.
  - Labels and HTML block names match without case for ASCII letters
    only; punctuation and white space are Mac Roman's.

Gemtext: text lines as lines (a blank line between paragraphs), "=>"
links one to a line (the address as the label if there's none),
"```" preformatted text (its alt text not shown), "#", "##", and "###"
headings, "* " list items, and ">" quotes.

Memory, for each page being read: about 19K for Markdown and 3.5K for
Gemtext, all taken at the start and given back at the page's end.

Written from the CommonMark specification (0.31.2), GitHub Flavored
Markdown's tables section, and the Gemini project's gemtext
specification.

Build: ./build.sh writes build/Modern Text.bin. Tests: tests/run.sh.
